      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "La última vez, Hiʻiaka llegó a Kauaʻi y vio el espíritu de Lohiʻau en la boca de una cueva.",
          "en": "Last time, Hiʻiaka reached Kauaʻi and saw Lohiʻau's spirit at the mouth of a cave."
        },
        {
          "es": "La gente le contó la verdad: Lohiʻau había muerto de tristeza, esperando a la mujer de Puna.",
          "en": "The people told her the truth: Lohiʻau had died of sorrow, waiting for the woman from Puna."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y dos mujeres moʻo habían escondido su cuerpo en lo alto del acantilado, y tenían atrapado su espíritu.",
          "en": "And two moʻo women had hidden his body high up on the cliff, and held his spirit captive."
        },
        {
          "es": "Westervelt dice que eran las mismas moʻo que Pele había humillado en la fiesta de hula.",
          "en": "Westervelt says they were the same moʻo women Pele had shamed at the hula feast."
        }
