          1.05
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Bajaron el cuerpo a una casa hecha de hojas de ti.",
          "en": "They carried the body down to a house made of ti leaves."
        },
        {
          "es": "Durante diez días, Hiʻiaka cantó los cantos que devuelven un espíritu a su cuerpo, mientras abajo la gente bailaba hula.",
          "en": "For ten days, Hiʻiaka chanted the chants that return a spirit to its body, while the people below danced hula."
        },
        {
          "es": "Wahineʻōmaʻo le frotaba los pies. El espíritu entró por las plantas de los pies, y subió despacio.",
          "en": "Wahineʻōmaʻo rubbed his feet. The spirit went in through the soles of his feet, and slowly rose."
        },
        {
          "es": "Al final, Lohiʻau respiró. Abrió los ojos. Estaba vivo.",
          "en": "At last, Lohiʻau took a breath. He opened his eyes. He was alive."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los tres bajaron sobre un arcoíris y se lavaron en el mar.",
          "en": "The three of them came down on a rainbow and washed themselves in the sea."
        }
      ],
