      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Hiʻiaka ya volvía con Lohiʻau. En Oʻahu cruzó la isla a pie, y subió a la cresta de Pōhākea.",
          "en": "Hiʻiaka was already on her way back with Lohiʻau. On Oʻahu she crossed on foot, and climbed the ridge of Pōhākea."
        },
        {
          "es": "Desde allí miró hacia su casa, más allá del mar. Y vio su bosque en llamas.",
          "en": "From there she looked toward her home, across the sea. And she saw her forest in flames."
        },
        {
          "es": "Vio a Hōpoe envuelta en lava.",
          "en": "She saw Hōpoe wrapped in lava."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hiʻiaka cantó un lamento: «Creí que mis lehua eran sagradas. Los pájaros de fuego se las comen».",
          "en": "Hiʻiaka chanted a lament: \"I thought my lehua were sacred. The birds of fire are eating them.\""
        },
        {
          "es": "Si fueras Hiʻiaka, ¿qué harías ahora?",
          "en": "If you were Hiʻiaka, what would you do now?"
